This lesson's exercises, slides, and sample datasets are adapted from the
IGV team's BroadE workshop materials:

Jim Robinson, Helga Thorvaldsdottir. Introduction to the Integrative
Genomics Viewer (IGV). BroadE Workshop, Broad Institute, April 2017.
https://www.igv.org/workshops/BroadApril2017/

The optional "Viewing Long-Read Sequencing Data" episode also adapts
examples and figures from:

Sirisha Hesketh. A guide to reviewing BAM files. EPI2ME Blog, Oxford
Nanopore Technologies, March 2024.
https://epi2me.nanoporetech.com/reviewing-bam/
Note: the screenshots reused from this post remain (c) Oxford Nanopore
Technologies plc and are not covered by this lesson's CC-BY license.

The same episode's hands-on inversion exercise streams public data
generated by the Genome in a Bottle Consortium. If you use this data,
please cite:

Zook JM, Catoe D, McDaniel J, et al. Extensive sequencing of seven human
genomes to characterize benchmark reference materials. Sci Data 3, 160025
(2016). https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2016.25

If you use IGV itself (the software) in published work, please cite it as
recommended at https://igv.org/, currently:

Robinson JT, Thorvaldsdottir H, Winckler W, Guttman M, Lander ES, Getz G,
Mesirov JP. Integrative Genomics Viewer. Nature Biotechnology 29, 24-26
(2011).

Thorvaldsdottir H, Robinson JT, Mesirov JP. Integrative Genomics Viewer
